sequenceDiagram
  %% process.stop on the Gateway engine: one `process` family on the Process's Node, one desired-state primitive for every runtime. Design for ADR 0267 and ADR 0271; no engine flow exists yet. Step names describe effects; the implementation settles action names unless an existing action is named.
  %% Rollout order: host systemd units first; Docker containers and Instance-container units join the same primitive later, each when its read-back is proven. Until a runtime is covered, its Process throws EngineUnsupported and runs on Swamp.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: process:stop
  %% kind: process.stop
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane EN icon=workflow pill=engine tone=purple
  %% lane N icon=server pill=executor tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=container tone=green
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant EN as Engine<br/>Gateway and NATS
  participant N as Target Node<br/>executor
  participant C as Instance copy<br/>via executor
  CLI->>GW: process:stop 417
  Note over GW: Validate, record the task<br/>Process 417: provisioning
  %%> Same admission as process/stop.mmd: access to the Process's Node, a Process not being removed; the intent carries unit or container name, runtime, on-demand flag and Instance container
  opt drain-waiting, Vite or release plan
    Note over GW: Refuse the engine<br/>EngineUnsupported
    %%> - a stop that waits for a drain, whatever its placement: a host systemd Process that runs Horizon (`GatewayHorizon::runs` with no Instance, whose unit carries the long-drain stop directives of SystemdProcessRenderer) and a Gateway release-container Process (Horizon, the scheduler)
    %%> - a Vite dev Process (`vite_plan`: dev route, listener, awake marker) and a production release layout
    %%> - decided at admission, before any order: the engine admits nothing, and the whole Operation takes the Swamp branch below
  end
  alt the engine admits the whole Operation
    %%> Admission, one decision per Operation (EngineKinds::routes):
    %%> - `process.stop` is in `ORBIT_ENGINE_KINDS`
    %%> - every Node a step touches reports its action in `$KV.NODES`: the `process` family's desired-state action (one name for start and stop)
    %%> - the flow accepts the plan shape; a part it does not cover throws `EngineUnsupported` before any order
    %%> - eligible plans, in rollout order: host systemd; then Docker; then a unit in an Instance container
    Note over GW: Bind steps, take the lock<br/>commit, publish the start
    %%> - the step rows and the Operation lock commit in one transaction before the start event; an Operation never moves between engines after this
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
    alt host systemd unit
      EN->>N: Converge the unit<br/>stopped · boot policy
      %%> Desired state: the unit is stopped and disabled at boot, as Swamp's `Set boot policy` / `Stop the Process` applies it; the admitted boot policy is an input of the step; an already-stopped unit only gets its boot policy
      %%> Target: the Process (`process-<id>`), so two orders for one Process run one after the other
    else Docker container, later
      EN->>N: Converge the container<br/>docker stop · stopped
      %%> `docker container stop` only when the state differs; an already-stopped container changes nothing
    else Instance container unit, later
      EN->>C: Converge the unit inside<br/>incus exec · systemctl
      %%> A nonblocking systemd job, then bounded readiness reads (5 s each, 10 tries 1 s apart), as `operation-process-container`; a stopped container fails the step, its next deployment starts it
    end
    alt host systemd unit
      N-->>EN: Observed state<br/>loaded · inactive · disabled
      %%> Read-back: LoadState=loaded, ActiveState=inactive (or failed after the stop), UnitFileState=disabled
    else Docker container, later
      N-->>EN: Observed state<br/>State.Status exited
      %%> Read-back: `docker inspect` State.Status is `exited`; `created` or any other status fails the step
    else Instance container unit, later
      C-->>EN: Observed state<br/>loaded · inactive · disabled
      %%> Read-back inside the copy: the same unit properties as on a host
    end
    %%> A mismatch fails the step (`process.state_mismatch`), as the native assert does; success is projected only from this read-back
    %%> `applied` is 0 when nothing changed, so a repeat after a crash reports the same end state
    opt the receipt is lost
      EN->>N: Resend the same step<br/>fresh nonce · same step ID
      %%> When:
      %%> - the step passes its resend deadline with no receipt; two sends, one execution
      %%> - the Operation keeps its lock, so Process 417 stays fenced; no other Operation and no Swamp run acts on it meanwhile
      %%> On the Node:
      %%> - the journal holds `done` for this Operation step, action and target: the executor answers the stored result with `repeat: true` and does not act again
      %%> - an order still `open` replays under the target lock first; an order that expired before the lock did nothing (`executor.order_expired`), and the step is sent again
      N-->>EN: Stored result<br/>repeat: true
    end
    alt every step verified
      EN->>GW: Record Process stopped<br/>desired state · status
      %%> - the kind's own projection records the result, the same rows a Swamp run records
    else a step fails
      EN--xGW: Failed step<br/>error_code · redacted detail
      %%> - a deterministic refusal is a terminal receipt too; the journal keeps it and a resend repeats it
      Note over GW: Mark the Process failed<br/>desired state unchanged
      %%> - no rollback and nothing to clean up; the same command converges again after the cause is fixed
    end
  else the engine does not admit it
    Note over GW: Start the Swamp run<br/>operation-process-stop
    %%> - the kind is not enabled, a Node lacks the action, `$KV.NODES` is unreadable, or the flow throws `EngineUnsupported`: the whole Operation runs operation-process-stop (process/stop.mmd)
    %%> - no step of it runs on the engine; an Operation never splits across engines
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
